  "reason": "The records collectively make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. R1 directly demonstrates SPS at 1000 °C for a mechanically alloyed, compositionally similar transition-metal HEA, while R3 uses SPS at 1050 °C on an especially close Al-Co-Fe-Ti-containing HEA and obtains a dense microstructure plus spinel formation. R2, R5, R6, R7, and R9 establish that mechanically alloyed BCC/refractory HEAs can be consolidated by SPS and commonly develop oxide or other secondary phases whose amount and properties depend on processing temperature. Separately, R12 and R13 supply the central oxidation rationale: protective oxide scales in related HEAs can produce diffusion-controlled parabolic kinetics, whereas R14 illustrates the consequences of nonprotective mixed oxides. Corrosion studies in chloride media and records involving phase-sensitive corrosion further support testing passive-film protection. The exact MgAlTiVFeCo composition, 1000 °C optimum, identified AlV2O4/FeAl2O4/FeTiO3 phases, and quantitative properties are not disclosed, but an expert could reasonably combine the close SPS precedent with the protective-oxide literature to propose the intervention and mechanism."
